### Aura — Auth API scratch file
# REST Client (.http) — click "Send Request" above each block.
#   VS Code:    install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
#   JetBrains:  built-in HTTP Client
#
# Endpoints per docs/INTEGRATION_PLAN.md §7b (Portal Gateway API).
# Base is plain HTTP (dev, no TLS) — do not send real/production credentials.
#
# Requests are in lifecycle order:
#   Register → OTP send → OTP verify → Login → Guest → Me → Refresh
#   → Change password → Logout.
# After Login/Register, copy access_token into @token before the bearer calls.

@baseUrl = http://169.58.184.121:30080/api/v1
@email = test1@example.com
@password = password
@username = test1

# Paste the access_token returned by Login/Register here, then run the bearer calls.
@token = eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJlOWMyNzI0Zi0wYjhiLTRlMGQtOGFkNy0yOWVmYjBlMTM0NDEiLCJzZXNzaW9uX2lkIjoiYzMyYzIxODEtMTVhOC00NjM3LTlmMDQtZDBkY2FlYmVhNjdiIiwiaWF0IjoxNzkxNDczNDQ3LCJleHAiOjE3OTE0NzQzNDcsInJvbGUiOiJ1c2VyIn0.ZccNjXWMPLXSI7WV7cX17alwwsgeWhQvaHL7uwN8J2o

# The 6-digit code from the verification email (for OTP verify).
@otp = 000000

# Paste the refresh_token returned by Login/Register here (for Refresh).
@refreshToken = PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE

@email_verification = aura_test_03@example.com

### 1. Register — create a new account
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### 2. OTP send — trigger/resend the verification email (bearer-scoped, needs @token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/otp/send
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "purpose": "email_verification"
}


### 3. OTP verify — confirm the email after Register (bearer-scoped, needs @token)
# Set @otp to the 6-digit code from the verification email.
POST {{baseUrl}}/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "code": "{{otp}}",
  "purpose": "email_verification"
}


### 4. Login — sign in with the account above
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


### 5. Login (wrong password) — expect 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "definitely-wrong"
}


### 6. Guest — anonymous session, no credentials
POST {{baseUrl}}/guest/create
Content-Type: application/json


### 7. Me — current user (needs a valid @token from Login/Register)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Me — current user (needs a valid @token from Login/Register)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Refresh — exchange a refresh token for a new access token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### 9. Change password — signed-in password change (bearer-scoped, needs @token)
# Field names are best-guess (serde snake_case) — adjust if the API rejects them.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "current_password": "{{password}}",
  "new_password": "NewPass1234!aA"
}


### 10. Logout — invalidate the current session (needs @token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
